.TH GIMMIX 1 "October 2026" "gimmix 0.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gimmix \- a graphical music player daemon (MPD) client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gimmix
.RB [ \-h ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gimmix
is a graphical client for the Music Player Daemon (MPD), written in C using
GTK+ 2. It has a compact mode with only the player controls and a full mode
with the current playlist, a library browser, the stored playlists, album
covers and lyrics.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print a summary of the options and exit.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B z
Previous song
.TP
.B x, c
Play or pause
.TP
.B v
Stop
.TP
.B b
Next song
.TP
.B i
Song information and tag editor
.TP
.B r
Toggle repeat
.TP
.B s
Toggle shuffle
.TP
.B l
Show or hide the playlist
.PP
The mouse wheel on the volume button or on the system tray icon changes the
volume.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The settings are stored in \fI$HOME/.gimmixrc\fR as \fIkey=value\fR lines
and are normally changed from the preferences dialog. On the first start a
dialog asks for the MPD connection.
.TP
\fBmpd_hostname\fR
Host name, IP address or UNIX socket path of the MPD server (default
localhost).
.TP
\fBmpd_port\fR
Port of the MPD server (default 6600).
.TP
\fBmpd_password\fR
Password for the MPD server. Leave blank for no password.
.TP
\fBmusic_directory\fR
The directory MPD plays from, the same as in mpd.conf. The tag editor needs
it to find the files, and the cover plugin looks there for images next to
the music.
.TP
\fBenable_systray\fR
Show a system tray icon (true or false, default true).
.TP
\fBenable_notification\fR
Show the currently playing song in the tray icon's tooltip (true or false,
default true).
.TP
\fBplay_on_add\fR
Start playing when a song is added to the playlist (default false).
.TP
\fBstop_on_exit\fR
Stop playback when gimmix quits (default false).
.TP
\fBenable_search\fR
Show the search box in the library browser (default true).
.TP
\fBupdate_on_startup\fR
Update the MPD database when gimmix starts (default false).
.TP
\fBcoverart_enable\fR
Show album covers (default true). Covers are taken from image files next to
the music or fetched from the Cover Art Archive and kept in
\fI$HOME/.gimmix/covers\fR.
.TP
\fBproxy_enable\fR, \fBproxy_host\fR, \fBproxy_port\fR
Use an HTTP proxy for fetching covers and lyrics.
.TP
\fBpl_column_title_show\fR, \fBpl_column_artist_show\fR,
\fBpl_column_album_show\fR, \fBpl_column_length_show\fR
Which columns the current playlist shows. Also available from the playlist's
context menu.
.TP
\fBfull_view_mode\fR, \fBwindow_xpos\fR, \fBwindow_ypos\fR,
\fBwindow_width\fR, \fBwindow_height\fR
The window mode, position and size. These are saved automatically when
gimmix quits.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $HOME/.gimmixrc
Configuration file.
.TP
.I $HOME/.gimmix/covers
Fetched album covers and the cover database.
.TP
.I $HOME/.gimmix/lyrics
Fetched lyrics.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mpd (1),
.BR mpd.conf (5)
.PP
